  "result": "Excellent! All 162 tests pass. Here's a summary of what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully added payment functionality to the invoicing system:\n\n### New Module: `src/payments.js`\n\n**`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`**\n- Records a payment on an invoice\n- Only works on invoices with status `'issued'` or `'partially_paid'`\n- Validates amount is a positive integer (in cents)\n- Prevents overpayments\n- Automatically updates invoice status to `'paid'` when fully paid, or `'partially_paid'` when partially paid\n- Creates the `payments` array if it doesn't exist\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with the updated invoice\n\n**`balanceDue(invoice)`**\n- Calculates the remaining balance (invoice total minus sum of all payments)\n- Returns 0 when fully paid\n\n### Error Codes Added to `src/errors.js`\n- `NOT_ISSUED`: Can only record payments on invoices with status \"issued\" or \"partially_paid\"\n- `OVERPAYMENT`: Payment amount exceeds the balance due\n\n### Test Suite: `test/payments.test.js`\n- 21 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Balance due calculations\n  - Single and multiple payments\n  - Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n  - Immutability verification\n  - All error cases (NOT_ISSUED, AMOUNT_INVALID, OVERPAYMENT)\n\nAll 162 tests pass, maintaining the existing 141 tests while adding 21 new ones for payments.",
